  "final_message": "Implemented all three versions. Each streams the log, validates each line, groups latencies by normalized path, and calculates nearest-rank percentiles for the ten busiest paths.\n\n- Rust uses compiled byte regexes, compact integer storage, and partial selection for percentiles.\n- `plain.py` uses standard-library byte regexes and sorts the selected paths\u2019 latencies.\n- `fast.py` stores ordinary latencies in compact arrays and uses NumPy partitioning; it falls back to arbitrary-precision integers for large values.\n\nAll three versions pass **s1, s2, and s3**. They also agree on additional checks covering empty input, malformed lines, path normalization, and very large latencies.",
